<title>GREECE: Greek capital mkt commissioner has not resigned.</title>
<headline>Greek capital mkt commissioner has not resigned.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The president of Greece's capital market commission Stavros Thomadakis has not resigned over remarks he made on Wednesday, his secretary told Reuters, denying market rumours.</p>
<p>Thomadakis warned on Wednesday against rumour-based investment decisions. Analysts said his remarks prompted a market selloff that took the general index down by more than 6.0 percent 20 minutes before the closing.</p>
<p>&quot;The market rumours are unfounded,&quot; she said. &quot;I can tell you that the president has not resigned and National Economy Minister Yannos Papandoniou was fully aware of the content of the statements made by Mr. Thomadakis.&quot;</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
